---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
import { VSCODE_EXTENSION_URL, GITHUB_URL } from '../../links';
---

<template lang="nmbl">
GuideLayout(title="Editor Support")
  section.guide-hero
    .container
      .breadcrumb
        | <a href="/guides">Guides</a> / Editor Support
      h1 Editor Support
      p.lead Syntax highlighting and IntelliSense for nmbl — wherever you write it.

  section.guide-content
    .container
      .content-grid
        aside.toc
          h3 Contents
          nav
            a(href="#vs-code") VS Code
            a(href="#what-you-get") What you get
            a(href="#other-editors") Other editors

        .prose
          Fragment:md
            ## VS Code

            The nmbl extension highlights `.nmbl` files, `<template lang="nmbl">`
            blocks in Vue / Svelte / Astro, and ``nmbl`…` `` tagged templates in
            `.ts` / `.tsx` / `.js` / `.jsx`, plus IntelliSense (completions,
            hover, go-to-definition, diagnostics) through a Volar language server.
          .editor-cta-row
            a.ext-cta(href={VSCODE_EXTENSION_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener")
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"/>
              <polyline points="7 10 12 15 17 10"/>
              <line x1="12" y1="15" x2="12" y2="3"/>
              </svg>
              | Install from the Marketplace
          Fragment:md
            ## What you get

            Highlighting works everywhere nmbl does. The depth of IntelliSense
            depends on the target — Vue is the most complete today:

            | Framework | Highlighting | IntelliSense |
            |---|---|---|
            | Vue | ✓ | Full type-checking via the dedicated Volar plugin |
            | Svelte / Astro | ✓ | Completions, hover, go-to-def via the nmbl language server (in `<template lang="nmbl">` blocks) |
            | React / Solid / Qwik | ✓ | Highlighting in ``nmbl`…` `` templates; richest tooling by factoring shared markup into a `.nmbl` file |
            | Standalone `.nmbl` | ✓ | Completions, hover, diagnostics |

            > A component's **own** props/emits aren't suggested yet in the
            > template — type them and rely on type-checking to validate.

            ## Other editors

            The language is defined **once** as a grammar (generating the
            TextMate and tree-sitter grammars) and the tooling is a standard Volar
            language server — both editor-agnostic. So support beyond VS Code is a
            matter of packaging, not new internals.

            Zed, JetBrains, and Neovim are on the roadmap. Want one prioritized, or
            running it elsewhere already?
          .editor-cta-row
            a.ext-cta.ext-cta-ghost(href={GITHUB_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener")
              | Open an issue on GitHub →
</template>

<style>
  .editor-cta-row {
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
  }

  .ext-cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.7rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: white;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background 0.2s;
  }

  .ext-cta:hover {
    background: var(--color-accent-hover);
  }

  .ext-cta-ghost {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .ext-cta-ghost:hover {
    background: transparent;
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
  }
</style>
